Open-source tool runs a 744B model on a 25GB machine with no GPU
2,242 Likes
You know that rule saying big AI models need big, expensive hardware? Colib=
ri just broke it. This open-source tool runs
GLM-5.2, a 744 billion parameter model
, on a regular laptop with only
25GB of RAM and no GPU
.
How? GLM-5.2 is a "Mixture of Experts" model, meaning it only activates a s=
mall slice of itself per response, roughly 40B out of 744B parameters. Coli=
bri keeps the always-needed core in RAM and streams the rest from your hard=
 drive on demand, like buffering a video instead of downloading it first.
Here is what this unlocks for you:
Run a frontier-class AI model locally, no cloud bill, no GPU required
OpenAI-compatible API
so your existing code just works
Conversations persist across restarts with zero re-processing
The cache learns your usage and gets faster over time
Speed is the honest tradeoff: cold starts hit roughly
0.05 to 0.1 tokens per second
, limited by disk read speed. A fast NVMe drive pushes that to 1 token per =
second or more. Slow, but free.
