<div style=3D"margin-top:0;">
<p>You know that rule saying big AI models need big, expensive hardware? Co=
libri just broke it. This open-source tool runs <b>GLM-5.2, a 744 billion p=
arameter model</b>, on a regular laptop with only <b>25GB of RAM and no GPU=
</b>.</p><p>How? GLM-5.2 is a "Mixture of Experts" model, meaning it only a=
ctivates a small slice of itself per response, roughly 40B out of 744B para=
meters. Colibri keeps the always-needed core in RAM and streams the rest fr=
om your hard drive on demand, like buffering a video instead of downloading=
 it first.</p><p>Here is what this unlocks for you:</p><ul><li>Run a fronti=
er-class AI model locally, no cloud bill, no GPU required</li><li><b>OpenAI=
-compatible API</b> so your existing code just works</li><li>Conversations =
persist across restarts with zero re-processing</li><li>The cache learns yo=
ur usage and gets faster over time</li></ul><p>Speed is the honest tradeoff=
: cold starts hit roughly <b>0.05 to 0.1 tokens per second</b>, limited by =
disk read speed. A fast NVMe drive pushes that to 1 token per second or mor=
e. Slow, but free.</p>
